  "equipment_type": "Electric meter (kWh / demand)",
  "applies_to": "E-Mon D-Mon Class 3200, 3400 and 5000 electric submeters with the BACnet option, and the older (legacy) Class 3000 and 5000 meters, which use the same object map.",
  "summary": "E-Mon Class 3200, 3400 and 5000 meters are kWh/demand submeters; with the BACnet option they act as B-SS devices on MS/TP or (3400/5000) BACnet IP. Each meter publishes 43 read-only analog inputs: energy delivered/received, real/reactive/apparent power, power factor, peak demand, per-phase current, voltage and phase angle, and two external pulse inputs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names are the Description column of the \"BACnet Object Descriptors\" tables; every object is a read-only analog input (Present Value).",
    "The same point-map document also gives Modbus and LonWorks maps; only the BACnet table for this meter family is listed here.",
    "PICS: MS/TP master at 9.6k, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8k bps, or BACnet IP; the Class 3200 meter does not support BACnet IP.",
    "AI 1-41 apply to all three classes; AI 42-43 (external inputs) are standard on the Class 5000 and part of the expanded feature package on the Class 3400, and are not available on the Class 3200.",
    "kWh/kVARh are cleared from the meter display (reset kW/kWh, jumper J6 closed), not over BACnet.",
    "Legacy Class 3000/5000 meters use the same 43 AIs except AI 9, which is \"Current total\" (A) instead of Peak demand. On legacy meters the totals can only be cleared over Modbus RTU (jumper J2 closed, BACnet IP module removed)."
  ],
